# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF, whatever the working copy
# uses. Go, YAML and Markdown are all happier with LF, and a repository that
# stores CRLF produces a diff on every file the first time somebody builds on
# Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are the exception: Windows PowerShell 5.1 mis-parses a
# script whose lines end in a bare LF in some hosting scenarios.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files must not be touched at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.db binary
